{"title":"Writing in the Progressive Form","puid":"c-nateng-2-gb/skr0ip","path":"/../c-nateng-2-gb/topic-05c-vgp-text/block-03-progressive-form/level-01","type":"normal","keyboardLayout":"standardNATENG","voiceLang":"en","voice":"f3_2025","instruction":{"voice":"m2_2025","speaker":true,"autoplay":true},"image":{"width":200},"trainers":[{"trainer":"dragMatch","instruction":{"text":"Match the sentences together. Look at the verb phrases to help."},"soundMode":"a","shuffleAtoms":true,"feedback":{"finish":{"text":"The <b>progressive form</b> describes something that is ongoing. The <b>progressive form</b> can be in the <t-pink>past</t-pink> and <t-cyan>present</t-cyan> tense. It is formed with the correct form of the verb <i>'to be'</i> in the correct tense, followed by an <i>-ing</i> verb.","speaker":true,"autoplay":true,"style":"avatar"}},"atoms":[{"a":"We <t-blue>play</t-blue> football.","b":"We <t-pink>are playing</t-pink> football."},{"a":"I <t-blue>did</t-blue> my homework.","b":"I <t-pink>was doing</t-pink> my homework."},{"a":"She <t-blue>listens</t-blue> to music.","b":"She <t-pink>is listening</t-pink> to music."},{"a":"They <t-blue>talked</t-blue> to each other.","b":"They <t-pink>were talking</t-pink> to each other."},{"a":"It <t-blue>rained</t-blue>.","b":"It <t-pink>was raining</t-pink>."}]},{"trainer":"buttons","instruction":{"text":"Decide if this sentence is in the <b><t-pink>past progressive</t-pink></b> form or the <b><t-cyan>present progressive</t-cyan></b> form."},"shuffleButtons":false,"shuffleAtoms":false,"soundMode":"a","atoms":[{"a":"I <b>was running</b> for the bus.","b":"++past present","image":"adobe_59148835","feedback":{"wrong":{"text":"This sentence is in the <b><t-pink>past</t-pink> progressive form</b> because it is talking about a continuous action that <b>already happened</b>.","speaker":true,"autoplay":true,"style":"avatar"}}},{"a":"They <b>are celebrating</b> Christmas together.","b":"past ++present ","image":"adobe_128170183_crop-273-0-3338-3338","feedback":{"wrong":{"text":"This sentence is in the <b><t-cyan>present</t-cyan> progressive form</b> because it is talking about a continuous action that is <b>happening right now</b>.","speaker":true,"autoplay":true,"style":"avatar"}}},{"a":"We <b>were welcoming</b> in the guests.","b":"++past present","image":"adobe_93430721","feedback":{"wrong":{"text":"This sentence is in the <b><t-pink>past</t-pink> progressive form</b> because it is talking about a continuous action that <b>already happened</b>.","speaker":true,"autoplay":true,"style":"avatar"}}},{"a":"She <b>is cleaning</b> her bedroom.","b":"past ++present ","image":"adobe_217406274","feedback":{"wrong":{"text":"This sentence is in the <b><t-cyan>present</t-cyan> progressive form</b> because it is talking about a continuous action that is <b>happening right now</b>.","speaker":true,"autoplay":true,"style":"avatar"}}}]}],"parentTopic":{"title":"Vocabulary, Grammar and Punctuation - Text","path":"/../c-nateng-2-gb/topic-05c-vgp-text/topic","puid":"c-nateng-2-gb/6c7tl9"},"parentBlock":{"title":"Progressive Form","path":"/../c-nateng-2-gb/topic-05c-vgp-text/block-03-progressive-form/block","puid":"c-nateng-2-gb/5d4z6t"},"mediaFiles":{"sounds":[{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/I <b>was running</b> for the bus.","etag":"ae9a-8973"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/I <t-blue>did</t-blue> my homework.","etag":"f733-8685"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/I <t-pink>was doing</t-pink> my homework.","etag":"abf9-10269"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/It <t-blue>rained</t-blue>.","etag":"4f57-5661"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/It <t-pink>was raining</t-pink>.","etag":"12e3-6381"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/She <b>is cleaning</b> her bedroom.","etag":"b553-11277"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/She <t-blue>listens</t-blue> to music.","etag":"4b90-9981"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/She <t-pink>is listening</t-pink> to music.","etag":"9319-10701"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/The <b>progressive form</b> describes something that is ongoing. The <b>progressive form</b> can be in the <t-pink>past</t-pink> and <t-cyan>present</t-cyan> tense. It is formed with the correct form of the verb <i>'to be'</i> in the correct tense, followed by an <i>-ing</i> verb.","etag":"6e07-72477"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/They <b>are celebrating</b> Christmas together.","etag":"b830-13005"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/They <t-blue>talked</t-blue> to each other.","etag":"9ad7-8397"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/They <t-pink>were talking</t-pink> to each other.","etag":"8f6c-9693"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/This sentence is in the <b><t-cyan>present</t-cyan> progressive form</b> because it is talking about a continuous action that is <b>happening right now</b>.","etag":"2956-39213"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/This sentence is in the <b><t-pink>past</t-pink> progressive form</b> because it is talking about a continuous action that <b>already happened</b>.","etag":"639e-35901"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/We <b>were welcoming</b> in the guests.","etag":"ca07-11277"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/We <t-blue>play</t-blue> football.","etag":"16a8-7677"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/We <t-pink>are playing</t-pink> football.","etag":"9566-8685"},{"fileId":"sound/en/m2_2025/Decide if this sentence is in the <b><t-pink>past progressive</t-pink></b> form or the <b><t-cyan>present progressive</t-cyan></b> form.","etag":"4846-31392"},{"fileId":"sound/en/m2_2025/Match the sentences together. Look at the verb phrases to help.","etag":"cb82-29952"}],"svgs":[],"lsgs":[],"images":[{"fileId":"image/adobe_128170183_crop-273-0-3338-3338","etag":"bc1c-45065","originalWidth":500,"originalHeight":500},{"fileId":"image/adobe_217406274","etag":"c232-52209","originalWidth":750,"originalHeight":500},{"fileId":"image/adobe_59148835","etag":"46b1-66273","originalWidth":750,"originalHeight":500},{"fileId":"image/adobe_93430721","etag":"3e68-42353","originalWidth":755,"originalHeight":500},{"fileId":"image/lsg_24637f46f5","etag":"7092-19370",